{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently underestimates immediate price spikes (e.g., +3-4 EUR) following recent highs, failing to capture the momentum of upward breaks.",
    "Adjust for excessive mean reversion: The model assumes a rapid return to a lower equilibrium (approx. 79-80 EUR) after volatility, whereas true outcomes exhibit a slower, more volatile decay or sustained higher levels before dropping.",
    "Invert sentiment lag: When sentiment history shows high values (0.67-1.00) coinciding with price peaks, the model incorrectly predicts a decline; instead, apply a positive bias to forecasts for the first 5-7 days to align with the delayed market reaction.",
    "Reduce forecast slope: The model's 30-day horizon forecasts show a monotonic, linear increase (or decrease) that ignores the cyclical nature of the data; flatten the forecast curve to match the observed oscillation between 75 and 85 EUR.",
    "Overshoot correction: After a price spike (e.g., >84 EUR), the model's subsequent forecasts drop too aggressively; reduce the rate of decline in the 10-20 day horizon to prevent underestimating the floor price."
  ]
}
